{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43202 - PROTEIN:6153",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One and Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. This compound appears to act as a target for multiple downstream molecules, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, and Botryorhodine C, all of which are themselves targets of the compound. These intermediates ultimately converge on Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, indicating a potential pathway where the compound may influence the activity of this enzyme through multiple intermediate steps. The shared target of these molecules points to a possible mechanism where 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One may modulate the activity of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like through a series of metabolic or enzymatic interactions. The evidence supports a role for this compound in regulating the activity of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
